---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SubNav from '../components/SubNav.astro';
import SubFooter from '../components/SubFooter.astro';
import EarlyNote from '../components/EarlyNote.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';

import hero from '../assets/pages/neighborhood-hero.jpg';
import morning from '../assets/pages/morning-market.jpg';
import midday from '../assets/pages/midday-street.jpg';
import afternoon from '../assets/pages/afternoon-garden.jpg';
import evening from '../assets/pages/evening-courtyard.jpg';
import longTable from '../assets/pages/long-table.jpg';

const description =
  'Neighborhood living, Now City style: a day in the life: morning market, walkable streets, gardens, courtyards, and neighbors by default.';
---

<Layout title="Living Here" description={description}>
  <SubNav current="/living-here" />

  <section class="pt-12 md:pt-16">
    <div class="container-wide">
      <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-md shadow-sm">
        <Image src={hero} alt="A residential street with gardens, play, and cafes woven between homes." widths={[800, 1400, 2200]} sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 1100px, 100vw" class="h-auto w-full object-cover" loading="eager" />
      </div>
      <div class="mt-10 max-w-3xl">
        <p class="eyebrow">Living Here</p>
        <h1 class="mt-4 font-display text-4xl leading-tight text-forest-700 md:text-5xl">A day here.</h1>
        <p class="lede mt-6">The easiest way to understand what we are building is to walk through one ordinary day in it. Concept renderings of our first neighborhood, now taking shape.</p>
        <EarlyNote variant="compact" title="A day we are designing toward." body="These are concept renderings of a neighborhood in planning, not photographs of a finished place. First homes are years out, and the details will keep changing." cta={false} />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-section">
    <div class="container-wide grid items-center gap-10 md:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-md shadow-sm"><Image src={morning} alt="A morning market hall with produce stalls and coffee." widths={[700, 1200, 2000]} sizes="(min-width: 768px) 50vw, 100vw" class="h-auto w-full" /></div>
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Morning</p>
        <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-3xl text-forest-700">Coffee, bread, produce, hello.</h2>
        <p class="prose-body mt-4">The market is three minutes from every front door, so breakfast is a walk, not a drive. The baker knows the regulars. The produce came from close by. The first hour of the day happens among neighbors instead of behind a windshield.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-section bg-cream-50">
    <div class="container-wide grid items-center gap-10 md:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="md:order-2 overflow-hidden rounded-md shadow-sm"><Image src={midday} alt="A green neighborhood street with playground, garden beds, cafes, and a fountain." widths={[700, 1200, 2200]} sizes="(min-width: 768px) 50vw, 100vw" class="aspect-[4/3] h-auto w-full object-cover" /></div>
      <div class="md:order-1">
        <p class="eyebrow">Midday</p>
        <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-3xl text-forest-700">Streets that do the raising with you.</h2>
        <p class="prose-body mt-4">Kids reach the playground without crossing traffic. Lunch tables spill out under awnings. Errands are a loop on foot, and the street itself, gardens, water, shade, play, does quiet work all day: cooling the block, soaking the storms, giving everyone a reason to linger.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-section">
    <div class="container-wide grid items-center gap-10 md:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-md shadow-sm"><Image src={afternoon} alt="Residents tending raised garden beds between homes." widths={[700, 1200, 2000]} sizes="(min-width: 768px) 50vw, 100vw" class="aspect-[4/3] h-auto w-full object-cover" /></div>
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Afternoon</p>
        <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-3xl text-forest-700">Gardens where the generations mix.</h2>
        <p class="prose-body mt-4">The beds between buildings belong to everyone: kids learning where food comes from, elders with the best tomato advice, and the casual supervision that makes a neighborhood safe without anyone patrolling it. Growing things together is the oldest social network there is.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-section bg-cream-50">
    <div class="container-wide grid items-center gap-10 md:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="md:order-2 overflow-hidden rounded-md shadow-sm"><Image src={evening} alt="A courtyard at dusk with landscape lighting and neighbors gathered." widths={[700, 1200, 1870]} sizes="(min-width: 768px) 50vw, 100vw" class="aspect-[4/3] h-auto w-full object-cover" /></div>
      <div class="md:order-1">
        <p class="eyebrow">Evening</p>
        <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-3xl text-forest-700">Dusk in the courtyard.</h2>
        <p class="prose-body mt-4">Dinner outside because it is easy. Music from the commons some nights, quiet most nights. The courtyard holds the day's last hour the way a living room holds a family, and nobody had to organize anything for it to happen.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-section">
    <div class="container-narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">Why it works</p>
      <h2 class="mt-4 font-display text-3xl text-forest-700 md:text-4xl">None of this is an accident.</h2>
      <div class="prose-body mt-6">
        <p>Days like this come from decisions made early: daily needs within a short walk, streets designed for people first, nature doing real infrastructure work, homes built healthy and efficient enough that comfort costs less. We design the whole neighborhood as one system, then deliver it in phases.</p>
        <p>The full thinking lives in <a href="/manifesto">the manifesto</a>, and the homes themselves have <a href="/homes">a page of their own</a>.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-10 overflow-hidden rounded-md shadow-sm"><Image src={longTable} alt="Neighbors sharing a meal at a long table." widths={[700, 1200, 1400]} sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 800px, 100vw" class="h-auto w-full object-cover" /></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-section bg-cream-50">
    <div class="container-wide">
      <div class="max-w-3xl">
        <p class="eyebrow">The Year Here</p>
        <h2 class="mt-4 font-display text-3xl text-forest-700 md:text-4xl">Four seasons of a place that keeps its rhythm.</h2>
        <p class="prose-body mt-5">A good neighborhood has a calendar the way a family does. Ours is being designed season by season, with the people who will live it.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-10 grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
        <div class="rounded-md border border-stone-100 bg-white p-6"><h3 class="font-display text-lg text-forest-700">Spring</h3><p class="prose-body mt-2 !text-[15px]">Planting weekends in the shared beds, the market spilling outdoors, bikes coming back out in force.</p></div>
        <div class="rounded-md border border-stone-100 bg-white p-6"><h3 class="font-display text-lg text-forest-700">Summer</h3><p class="prose-body mt-2 !text-[15px]">Long evenings in the courtyard, music on the commons, splash plazas working overtime, dinner outside as the default.</p></div>
        <div class="rounded-md border border-stone-100 bg-white p-6"><h3 class="font-display text-lg text-forest-700">Fall</h3><p class="prose-body mt-2 !text-[15px]">Harvest tables, the market at its fullest, maker workshops moving indoors, the streets gold for a month.</p></div>
        <div class="rounded-md border border-stone-100 bg-white p-6"><h3 class="font-display text-lg text-forest-700">Winter</h3><p class="prose-body mt-2 !text-[15px]">The cozy season: warm halls, lit windows, saunas and soups, and neighbors close enough that nobody hibernates alone.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="mx-auto mt-12 max-w-3xl">
        <p class="eyebrow">Belonging</p>
        <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-2xl text-forest-700">Community is designed for, then grown.</h3>
        <p class="prose-body mt-4">The buildings can only set the table. The life comes from clubs that start in someone's kitchen, traditions that begin as one good idea, and the slow accumulation of familiar faces. Our part is to make room for all of it: the long tables, the workshop, the stage, the garden, and a steward who stays, tending the place for decades rather than flipping it in years. Your part, if you want one, starts with <a href="/#follow-along">a name on the list</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <SubFooter />
</Layout>
